---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layouts.astro";
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";

const entries = await getCollection("learningLog");

entries.sort((a, b) => 
    b.data.date.getTime() - a.data.date.getTime()
);
---
<Layout title = "Learning Log | Olivia McFadden">
    <section class="learning-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">LEARNING LOG</p>
        <h1>Documenting the process, not just the outcome.</h1>

        <p class="text">
            A record of what I'm learning, what I'm building, and how my approach develops over time.
        </p>
    </section>
    <section class="updates">
        <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="eyebrow">WEEKLY UPDATES</p>
            <h2>Recent Entries</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="entries">
            {entries.map((entry) => (
                <a
                    href={`/learning/${entry.id}`}
                    class="entry-card"
                >
                    <p class="entry-date">
                        {entry.data.date.toLocaleDateString("en-GB", {
                            day: "numeric",
                            month: "long",
                            year: "numeric",
                        })}
                    </p>

                    <h3>{entry.data.title}</h3>

                    <p class = "entry-description">{entry.data.description}</p>

                    <span class="read-more">
                        Read entry →
                    </span>
                </a>
            ))}
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="about-log">
        <h2>Why I'm Keeping a Learning Log</h2>

        <p class="text">
            This log is more for myself, to keep track of my own progress, but I 
            figured it would be useful to put it on here so that others can see my thoughts and process as 
            I continue my learning journey. I intend to update this weekly - some weeks may be more 
            productive than others (the wonderful life of being a uni student), but I think it would be 
            really great to be able to look back on everything I have learned.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="how-i-work">
        <h2>My Style of Working</h2>
        <p class = "bold"> Coding </p>
        <p class = "text">
            At the moment, my main approach to coding is always to make things as easy and simple as 
            possible - mainly for the sake of future me, or anyone else who looks at my code. For me, this 
            looks like having plenty of concise comments which explain what the code does and why it's there.
            I find that writing these comments makes sure I actually understand the code I'm writing, because 
            it forces me to explain what's going on, and makes it so much easier to come back to. It's really
            important to me that I understand what my code does - I find it is so much easier to pinpoint errors
            and make tweaks when I know what I'm looking for.
            <br>
            <br>
            When it comes to Python stuff, I always prefer to use a Jupyter Notebook. I like being able to 
            break the code up into cells, and having the option of writing markdown cells - this way I can give
            an overview of what the coding cells do, and use comments to explain specific lines of code. I also
            feel like being able to break parts up into individual cells makes a project much more readable -
            I'm not big on having big blocks of code.
        </p>
    </section>
</Layout>

<style>
    .learning-header {
        padding: 1rem 0 1rem;
    }

    .eyebrow {
        color: var(--accent);
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        letter-spacing: 0.15em;
        font-weight: 600;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }

    h1 {
        font-size: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6rem);
        line-height: 1;
        letter-spacing: -0.04em;
        margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    }

    .text {
        color: var(--secondary);
        font-size: 1.05rem;
        line-height: 1.5;        
    }

    .bold {
        font-weight: bold;
        color: black;
    }    

    .page-header > p:last-child {
        color: var(--secondary);
        font-size: 1.15rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
    }

     .entries {
        padding-bottom: 1rem;
    }

    .section-label {
        color: var(--accent);
        font-size: 0.75rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        letter-spacing: 0.15em;
        margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }

    .entries {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
    }

    .entry-card {
        padding: 1rem 1rem;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--border);

        text-decoration: none;
        color: inherit;

        transition: background 0.2s ease;
    }

    .entry-card:last-child {
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }

    .entry-card:hover {
        background: var(--surface);
    }

    .entry-date {
        color: var(--accent);
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        font-weight: 600;
    }

    h2 {
        font-size: 1.8rem;
        letter-spacing: -0.02em;
        margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
        margin-top: 2rem
    }

    .entry-description {
        color: var(--secondary);
        line-height: 1.6;
        max-width: 650px;
        margin: 0 0 1rem;
    }

    .read-more:hover {
        color: var(--accent);
    }


    @media (max-width: 600px) {
        .entry-card {
            grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
            gap: 1rem;
        }

        h2 {
            font-size: 1.5rem;
        }

    }
</style>